# Next.js Portal

## Components

- Prefer Server Components by default.
- Client Components only for interactivity.
- Client code must never import Prisma, secrets, private keys, or Nest modules.
- Use App Router. Consider `loading.tsx` / `error.tsx` / `not-found.tsx` on major routes.
- Prefer server data loading; avoid unnecessary client fetching.
- Large lists: backend pagination/filtering only.

## Design system

Enterprise SaaS look. Extend existing shadcn / `@workspace/ui` — do not invent competing primitives.

Do: clean typography, consistent spacing, strong hierarchy, professional tables, responsive layouts, accessible forms, controlled empty/loading/error/success states.

Avoid: excessive gradients, huge cards, random colors, clutter, basic HTML forms, animation noise.

## Tables & search

Server-side pagination, search, filter, sort. Debounced search. Index-backed fields (survey id, owner, mobile, parcel, property no, ward, locality). Never load 100K rows into the browser.

## Forms

Schema validation, field errors, preserve values, prevent double submit, loading + success feedback. Survey sections: Basic / Owner / Respondent / Property / Classification / Measurements / Utilities / Attachments.

## A11y & i18n

Keyboard, labels, focus, semantic HTML, contrast. Preserve Hindi/Unicode — never strip or auto-transliterate. Localization-ready (Hindi/English). Desktop-first; tablet/mobile usable.
